          "id": "GENUS_AUSTRALOPITHECUS",
          "name": "Australopithecus",
          "rank": "GENUS",
          "description": "Extinct bipedal hominins from Africa, living roughly 2–4 million years ago. Australopithecus walked upright but retained many ape-like features including small brains and long arms. The famous fossil 'Lucy' (A. afarensis) is among the best-known human ancestors, demonstrating that upright walking preceded the evolution of large brains.",
